      "why": "Fully pipelined gives 1 result/cycle, so at Fmax >= 32 MHz it meets throughput_msps >= 32. Latency is N+2 cycles; with N in 12..20 and Fmax >= 32 MHz, latency is 14..22 cycles = 0.44..0.69 us. The p99_batch constraint (0.5 us) is tight: the 32 requests arrive at once, so the last result exits at (N+2) cycles after the tick. At 32 MHz, 15 cycles = 0.469 us passes, 16 cycles = 0.5 us is borderline. So N must be low enough that (N+2)/Fmax <= 0.5 us, i.e. N+2 <= 0.5e-6 * Fmax. For Fmax=32 MHz, N+2 <= 16, so N <= 14. For Fmax=40 MHz, N+2 <= 20, so N <= 18. The accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-12 = 0.000244 requires enough iterations and guard bits. With data_width=16, n_iter=14, angle_guard=1, frac_guard=1, rounding=round, accuracy should be around 14-15 bits. I focus on the low-N, moderate-width region where the batch latency constraint is satisfiable. data_width 14..18 covers the accuracy requirement (16 is the natural fit for 12-bit error with margin). n_iter 12..20 spans the latency/accuracy trade-off. angle_guard 0..2 and frac_guard 0..2 give the accuracy margin without excessive area."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec requires throughput >= 32 Msps and p99 batch latency <= 0.5 us for 32 simultaneous requests. The pipelined family is the natural fit: it produces 1 result/cycle, so throughput = Fmax. The critical constraint is the batch latency: all 32 requests arrive at the tick, and the last one exits after N+2 cycles. So (N+2)/Fmax <= 0.5 us. This couples N and Fmax tightly. For the minimum-area design, I want the smallest N and data_width that meet max_abs_err <= 2^-12. With rounding=round and modest guards, n_iter=14 with data_width=16 should give ~14-bit accuracy. The Fmax must then be >= (N+2)/0.5us = 2*(N+2) MHz. For N=14, Fmax >= 32 MHz. I search n_iter 12..20 to find the sweet spot where the area (which grows with N and data_width) is minimized while both the accuracy and batch-latency constraints are met. data_width 14..18 brackets the minimum width that achieves 12-bit accuracy with the chosen guards. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0..2) to limit area while providing the accuracy margin. I allocate all budget to pipelined since pipelined_m with m>1 would have the same per-cycle throughput but higher latency (ceil(N/m)+2), making the batch constraint harder to meet, and m=1 is just pipelined. So pipelined is the only viable family for this spec's tight batch-latency constraint."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established and robust. The minimum area design (39,973 um^2) comfortably satisfies the throughput constraint (132 MSPS >= 32) and the accuracy constraint (12.53 bits > 12 bits). The system constraint (sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us) is also met with a margin (best seen 0.282 us). The front covers a reasonable range of accuracy (12.5 to 14.2 bits) against area (39,973 to 49,611 um^2). Since this is the final round and the current front provides a clear, feasible solution that minimizes area while meeting all constraints, stopping is the appropriate action. The selection rule (min area) will pick the 39,973 um^2 design, which is a valid and efficient solution."
